    "maker": "Hannah Whitall Smith",
    "date": "1875",
    "quote": "Most Christians are like a man who was toiling along the road, bending under a heavy burden, when a wagon overtook him, and the driver kindly offered to help him on his journey. He joyfully accepted the offer, but when seated, continued to bend beneath his burden, which he still kept on his shoulders. \"Why do you not lay down your burden?\" asked the kind-hearted driver. \"Oh!\" replied the man, \"I feel that it is almost too much to ask you to carry me, and I could not think of letting you carry my burden too.\" And so Christians, who have given themselves into the care and keeping of the Lord Jesus, still continue to bend beneath the weight of their burden, and often go weary and heavy-laden throughout the whole length of their journey.",
